            <common:generalComment xml:lang="en">The liquefaction process of air represent an average cryogenic air separation process. As products only liquid nitrogen, liquid oxygen and liquid crude argon were considered. No gaseous product considered. The allocation factors were calculated from the heat of vaporisation and the specific heat capacity multiplied with the temperature difference from 20°C to the boiling point. Multi output process. The allocated outputs are liquid nitrogen, liquid oxygen and liquid crude argon.;
Formula: N2, O2, Ar; 
